course: dictionary
lesson: 10616
title: Unevenly: not equal or smooth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unevenly is an adverb. An adverb tells you how something happens or is done. It means not in an equal or smooth way: some parts get more and some get less, or a surface is bumpy instead of flat.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «Sam shared the sweets unevenly, so one friend got eight and the other got two.» Shared equally would mean the same number each, so unevenly must mean not the same. Test it: swap in "not equally" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The same idea works in other subjects. «Winds start because the Sun warms the Earth unevenly.» The Sun does not warm every part of the Earth in the same way, and that difference makes the air move. In art, paint spread unevenly has thick patches and thin patches.
fact: Unevenly means not in an equal or smooth way.
fact: An adverb is a word that tells you how, when or where something happens, and unevenly tells you how.
fact: «Shared unevenly» in maths means the groups are not equal, so it is not a fair share.
fact: «Ordinary glass can crack when heated or cooled unevenly.» Different parts change temperature at different speeds, so they do not change evenly.
fact: Opposite of unevenly is evenly: equal, smooth, or the same all over.
exercise: What does unevenly mean? | In a loud voice | Again and again, many times | Very quickly | *Not in an equal or smooth way
exercise: «Sam shared the sweets unevenly, so one friend got eight and the other got two.» Why is this not a fair share? | *Because the groups are not equal | Because Sam ate some of them | Because there were too many sweets | Because the sweets were all green
exercise: People are unevenly spread across a country. Which word means the opposite of unevenly? | Slowly | *Equally | Loudly | Badly
test: «Microwaves make water molecules wiggle very fast, which heats the food, often unevenly, so stirring halfway mixes hot and cooler parts.» Why do we stir food halfway through? | Because the food needs to be painted | *Because the food heats unevenly, so stirring mixes hot and cooler parts | Because stirring makes the microwave spark | Because stirring makes the food colder
test: Ellie painted the wall and the paint went on unevenly, with thick patches and thin patches. What does unevenly describe? | *The way the paint was spread | The size of the wall | The time of day Ellie painted | The colour of the paint
exam: In «Winds start because the Sun warms the Earth unevenly.», what kind of word is unevenly? | An adjective, because it describes the Earth | A verb, because it shows an action | A noun, because it names a thing | *An adverb, because it tells how the Sun warms the Earth
